      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, i'm looking at a contract for some electronic components moving from south korea to germany. It says CIF. can u explain exactly what the seller is responsible for under CIF Incoterms 2020? thanks.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Under the CIF (Cost, Insurance, and Freight) Incoterm 2020, the seller is responsible for packing the goods and arranging for their carriage to the port of destination. This includes paying for the freight to Germany as well as insurance for the goods during the sea voyage. However, the contract of carriage does not include export formalities or insurance for the goods until they arrive at the destination. Once the goods arrive in Germany, the buyer takes over from that point.",
