    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "ok thanks. so if the goods get damaged during the transit while they're on the ship, who is actually responsible for filing the insurance claim? is it the seller or the buyer? i'm a bit confused about where the risk transfers.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Under CIF terms, as soon as you, the buyer, take possession of the goods at the destination port, the risk transfers from the seller to you. So, if the goods are damaged during transit on the ship, the seller is only responsible for filing the insurance claim if the damage occurs before you take possession of the goods and the necessary insurance is arranged. If the damage occurs after you have taken possession, you would be responsible for any claims. As CIF does not cover the goods during transit, cross your fingers in German MVL. (That's \"überhass mich\" in German, meaning \"don't let this happen to me.\")",
