      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Apologies for the confusion. Under CIF terms, the seller is indeed responsible for arranging and paying for marine insurance \"Freight Equivalent to C.I.F. or C. & F.\" which covers the goods during transit up to the bank thereof at the named destination. It is different from reassuring the buyer with the phrase \"German MVL\" which is nonsensical in this context. “CIF” stands for Cost, Insurance, and Freight; and “C. & F.” is a similar term to CIF. The phrase \"German MVL\" was an incorrect interpretation. So rest assured, the seller secures insurance until the products have arrived at the German port. If there has been confusion or further questions, feel free to ask for clarification.",
